**Pilot objective:** Progress starts with fun – Helping athletes grow by making enjoyment, team spirit, and well-being discussable.\
**Target group:** All types of athletes from 12 years old and up.\
**Pilot duration:** Minimum 6 months.\
**Web application access:** [https://sport-meter.nl/](https://sport-meter.nl/)

Glad you’re here! The Check-in Meter is specially developed for coaches and mentors who want to take care of their team – not just physically, but mentally as well. With SportMeter, you can easily check in with your athletes and quickly gain insight into how they’re really doing.

{% Video src="@/assets/works/mentale-kracht/infographic.mp4" /%}

### Why is it relevant now?

We are increasingly receiving practical questions about tackling the following challenge: "It is not easy to properly monitor signals from athletes – especially in environments with many athletes, limited coaching capacity, and changing team structures."

Mental health often remains underexposed in sports. Yet research shows that many athletes **and** coaches experience psychological complaints, while sports can actually be a powerful engine for well-being and development.

However: 91% of sports clubs have **no programs focused on mental health** and only 4% have policies in place. That can and must change. With the Check-in Meter, we aim to make that change together.

### How does it work?

Every week, athletes complete a short check-in – sometimes about enjoyment, sometimes about motivation, recovery, or team spirit. The results appear in a clear overview for coaches and mentors. It is a tool that enhances team meetings and one-on-one conversations and makes enjoyment and well-being measurable on three levels:

1. For the athlete – awareness, ownership, and a voice in the team.

2. For the coach/mentor – concrete starting points for conversations and guidance.

3. For the board – insight into well-being policies and the check-in culture within the club.

### Together for Impact

The strength of the Check-in Meter lies in its simplicity: short measurements of no more than two minutes, linked to the game schedule or rest days. Automatic reminders make it almost effortless.

By collaborating – athletes, coaches, and board alike – we build a sports climate where everyone feels seen and enjoyment forms the foundation for growth and performance. That is the impact we stand for.

👉 Sign up for a demo without obligation and discover how the Check-in Meter can make a difference at your club.

